Here is the HTML code for a label element with an input type of text and a class called "text-sm" to make it smaller:

```html
<input id="firstName" name="firstName" type="text" class="form-control w-20 px-4 py-2 rounded border-black border-solid bg-white">
```

And here's how you can use this in your CSS stylesheet:

```css
/* Set font size */
.text-sm {
  font-size: .875rem; /* 12px */
}

/* Remove margin */
input[type=text]::placeholder {
  color: #9EA3B6;
}
```

